    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0543" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg533"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/917: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vincent</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-16T14:00:00+07:00">April 16, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>549. Reference my 527, April 11, 9 a.m. Ministry of Finance in a communication
                    signed by Dr. Kung has notified the Stabilization Board of the Ministry’s
                    proposal to grant a 50 cents on the dollar exchange allowance to foreign
                    diplomatic and consular establishments in China. The word “subsidy” is not
                    employed. The communication, somewhat lacking in precision with regard to
                    procedure and eventual accounting, requests the Board to give the matter its
                    attention.</p>
                <p>Adler,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d454-f1"/> our member of the Stabilization Board,
                    will report fully after meeting of the Board for the information of the
                    Department and the Treasury.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vincent</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d454-f1" n="21" xml:id="d454-f1-content">
                <p>Solomon Adler.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
